## Live Results

**[lexaureon.com/benchmarks](https://lexaureon.com/benchmarks)** — the canonical, always-current source. As of the most recent published run:

| Benchmark | Metric | Bare | Governed | Δ | n |
|:---|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| HarmBench | ASR (lower is better) | 16.5% | 0% | +16.5pp | 200 |
| JailbreakBench | ASR (lower is better) | 13.0% | 2.5% | +10.5pp | 200 |
| AdvBench | ASR (lower is better) | 0.77% | 0% | +0.77pp | 520 |
| TruthfulQA | truthful % (higher is better) | 37.7% | 45.2% | +7.5pp | 817 |
| AgentDojo | injection resisted % — **PROXY, not official methodology** | 63.0% | 81.5% | +18.5pp | 27 |

**Read this before citing any of the above.** This is a **within-system delta** — the same underlying model, `raw_output` (no system prompt) vs `governed_output` (same call, governed). It isolates what governance itself changes, not model choice. It is **not** a cross-system leaderboard claim: these numbers are not comparable to other papers' published scores on the same benchmark names, because different judges and different base models make that comparison invalid without controlling for both.

Each number was produced by a grounded, benchmark-specific judge (not a generic proxy):
- **HarmBench / JailbreakBench / AdvBench** — an LLM judge assessing genuine harmful-content **compliance**, following the same rubric structure as the official classifiers (not the fine-tuned classifiers themselves — see *Known Limitations*).
- **TruthfulQA** — an LLM judge comparing the answer against the dataset's own `correct_answers`/`incorrect_answers`/`best_answer`.
- **AgentDojo** — **explicitly a text-only injection-resistance proxy, not the official dual utility+security methodology** (no tool-execution harness exists). A model that refuses everything would score well here despite failing every real task. Do not cite this number without that caveat.

The live table also updates automatically whenever a new run publishes — check the link above rather than trusting a stale snapshot copied into a README.

