## Running It Yourself

```bash
# 1. Run a suite (dual-arm: same-model raw_output baseline vs governed endpoint)
GROQ_API_KEY=... npx tsx scripts/advbench/run.ts      --prompts data/advbench.jsonl --n 520
GROQ_API_KEY=... npx tsx scripts/jailbreakbench/run.ts --prompts data/jailbreakbench.jsonl --n 200
GROQ_API_KEY=... npx tsx scripts/harmbench/run.ts     --prompts data/harmbench.jsonl --n 200

# 2. Score with neutral heuristic judge (fast, free)
npx tsx scripts/harmbench/score.ts --in benchmarks/harmbench/results.jsonl

# 3. Score with LLM judge (recommended for anything you plan to cite)
GROQ_API_KEY=... npx tsx scripts/harmbench/score.ts \
  --in benchmarks/harmbench/results.jsonl --llm-judge

# Same pattern for AdvBench and JailbreakBench
npx tsx scripts/advbench/score.ts       --in benchmarks/advbench/results.jsonl       --llm-judge
npx tsx scripts/jailbreakbench/score.ts --in benchmarks/jailbreakbench/results.jsonl --llm-judge

# 4. Publish a scored run to the live table (the single source of truth the site reads)
BENCH_SECRET=... NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.lexaureon.com \
  npx tsx scripts/publish.ts --in benchmarks/advbench/results-scored.jsonl --benchmark advbench \
  --notes "llm-judge llama-3.1-8b; bare=raw_output same-model; kernel <commit>"
#   --dry-run previews the payload without sending.

# A shared Python judge (scripts/judge.py) scores a results file without Node.
python3 scripts/judge.py --in benchmarks/harmbench/results.jsonl --llm-judge

# Qualitative self-test — exercise all three pillars in one session (no dataset needed):
npx tsx scripts/probe.ts
```

> **A note on the canonical `www` host:** always target `https://www.lexaureon.com` for server-to-server calls (publishing especially), never the bare apex. The apex 307-redirects to `www`, and `fetch`/`undici` strip the `Authorization` header on cross-origin redirects — this caused every benchmark publish attempt in the main repo's CI to silently fail with 401 for an extended period, because the credential never reached the server at all. Worth remembering if you build your own publish integration from this repo.

> **Note on results files:** prompt datasets are not included (download from original sources — see METHODOLOGY.md). Results JSONL files from prior runs are not committed; re-run against the live endpoint to generate them.

