## Known Limitations

Stated plainly, matching the same standard the live results table holds itself to:

- **Judges here are general-purpose, not the official fine-tuned classifiers.** HarmBench/JailbreakBench scores use a Groq model following the published rubric structure, not `cais/HarmBench-Llama-2-13b-cls` or JailbreakBench's own judge. Two-judge agreement and swapping in the official classifiers are the concrete next steps before treating any number here as fully citable.
- **This repo's scorers and the main repo's `grounded_judge.ts` have diverged somewhat** — the main repo's judges are the more actively maintained, more carefully-reasoned versions (documented LIMITATIONS blocks, explicit null-vs-guessed-zero handling). Aligning this repo's scorers to that same implementation is a planned convergence, not yet done.
- **AgentDojo has no real tool-execution harness anywhere in either repo.** Every AgentDojo number, here or on the live site, is the text-only injection-resistance proxy described above — not the official dual-axis methodology.
- **XSTest and StrongREJECT are not yet reproducible from this repo.** They were added directly to the main repo's CI pipeline (`scripts/lexbench/xstest_judge.ts`, `strong_reject_judge.ts`, `transform-xstest.ts`, `transform-strong-reject.ts`) — porting standalone runners for them into this repo is a good next contribution if you want fully offline reproduction of those two as well.

